{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-fb623cb8-56c7-4905-9ab3-e178a9b2511c-0\nfc_a2d0c02a-0cd3-9a38-a460-c904f3a98e5c_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"git merge --no-edit main && loom data show MARATHON-3 --output json && loom data comments MARATHON-3 2>/dev/null || loom data show MARATHON-3 --output json | head -c 50000","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-fb623cb8-56c7-4905-9ab3-e178a9b2511c-0\nfc_a2d0c02a-0cd3-9a38-a460-c904f3a98e5c_0","simpleCommands":["git","loom","loom","loom","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"git","args":[{"type":"word","value":"merge"},{"type":"word","value":"--no-edit"},{"type":"word","value":"main"}],"fullText":"git merge --no-edit main"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-3"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-3 --output json"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"comments"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-3"}],"fullText":"loom data comments MARATHON-3"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-3"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-3 --output json"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"number","value":"50000"}],"fullText":"head -c 50000"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Merge main and show task JSON","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"b8e62675-1c0a-43a6-b50e-0b06cb55e7dc","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"git merge --no-edit main && loom data show MARATHON-3 --output json && loom data comments MARATHON-3 2>/dev/null || loom data show MARATHON-3 --output json | head -c 50000","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"Already up to date.\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-3\",\n  \"title\": \"Auth: register, login, me, bearer tokens\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"assignee\": \"frontend-dev-1\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"backend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMARATHON-3 implements cluster-wide authentication for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, plus the shared durable user/token store that all three HTTP nodes read and write. It establishes the `UserObj` identity shape, opaque bearer tokens (`Authorization: Bearer …`), password hashing, username slug validation, and a reusable auth middleware that every later authenticated route (workspaces, channels, WS, IRC `PASS`, SPA) will call. Without this seam, no other feature can attribute callers or survive a request to a different node.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n- **Runtime:** Stay on the MARATHON-2 stack: Node.js stdlib `http` router in `server/index.js`, no Express/Fastify required.\\n- **Durable shared store:** One **SQLite** database file at `/app/data/huddle.db`, opened by each HTTP worker via Node’s built-in **`node:sqlite` (`DatabaseSync`)**. Enable **WAL** + a non-zero `busy_timeout` so concurrent register/login from nodes 0/1/2 serialize safely. This is the authoritative store for users and sessions; **Redis is not used for auth durability** (Redis may be killed; users/tokens must survive).\\n- **Passwords:** `crypto.scrypt` with a per-user random salt; store only `password_salt` + `password_hash` (never plaintext). Compare with timing-safe equality.\\n- **Tokens:** Opaque random strings from `crypto.randomBytes` (≥16 chars when encoded; generate **32 bytes → base64url ≈ 43 chars**). Persist token → `user_id` in SQLite. Each successful register/login **issues a new token** (multiple concurrent sessions allowed). Tokens are looked up as presented; no JWT.\\n- **IDs:** Stable cluster-wide `user.id` via `crypto.randomUUID()` (string UUID).\\n- **Auth helper:** Export `authenticateRequest(req) → user | null` and/or middleware used by `/api/auth/me` and reserved for MARATHON-4+.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\\n|-------------|--------------|\\n| Redis HASH for users/tokens | Not durable across Redis SIGKILL; epic requires cluster to keep working when Redis dies |\\n| Per-node in-memory maps | Breaks “shared durable store across all three nodes”; register on :8000 would 401 on :8001 |\\n| JWT without server-side session | Harder to revoke; contract only needs opaque bearer length ≥16; SQLite session rows are simpler and match IRC/WS token checks later |\\n| npm `better-sqlite3` / Express | Unnecessary dependency; `node:sqlite` is available on Node 24 in this environment |\\n| JSON file + flock only | Workable but weaker concurrency and no unique indexes for username race → prefer SQLite UNIQUE |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\nSQLite file locking under three processes is simpler than a real DB server, but write throughput under heavy concurrent register is limited by WAL/busy waits. Acceptable for marathon scale. Using experimental `node:sqlite` avoids npm install in air-gapped/self-contained constraints; if the API shifts, implementer may pin Node flags or swap to an equivalent sync SQLite binding **without changing the HTTP contract**.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited from MARATHON-2 (authoritative)\\n| Convention | Value |\\n|------------|--------|\\n| App root | `/app` |\\n| HTTP entry | `server/index.js`, `NODE_ID` / `PORT` |\\n| Durable root | `/app/data/` |\\n| API prefix | `/api/...` |\\n| JSON | `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8` |\\n| Health | Unchanged; still Redis-independent |\\n\\n### Conventions fixed here (for siblings)\\n| Convention | Value |\\n|------------|--------|\\n| DB path | `/app/data/huddle.db` (create parent dir if missing) |\\n| `UserObj` public fields | `{id, username, display_name, timezone, avatar_url, status_text, status_emoji}` — always present on auth responses |\\n| Username rules | Regex `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$` (letters, digits, underscore only; no spaces/hyphens/dots) |\\n| Username uniqueness | Case-insensitive (`LOWER(username)` UNIQUE); store username with original casing from register |\\n| Password | UTF-8 string length ≥ 8 (code units / JS `.length`); no other complexity rules |\\n| Bearer | Header `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` (single space); token string length ≥ 16 |\\n| Error JSON | `{ \\\"error\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\" }` for 400/401/409 (message text open; must be non-empty) |\\n| No email | Register/login bodies must not require `email`; ignore unknown fields |\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Shared: `UserObj` (public; never include password/hash/salt/token)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid-string\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"username\\\": \\\"\\u003cslug\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"display_name\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"timezone\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"avatar_url\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"status_text\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"status_emoji\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n| Field | Type | Nullability | Default on register |\\n|-------|------|-------------|---------------------|\\n| `id` | string (UUID) | required | generated |\\n| `username` | string | required | from body |\\n| `display_name` | string | required in responses | `display_name` if provided non-empty, else copy of `username` |\\n| `timezone` | string | required in responses | `\\\"UTC\\\"` |\\n| `avatar_url` | string | required in responses | `\\\"\\\"` |\\n| `status_text` | string | required in responses | `\\\"\\\"` |\\n| `status_emoji` | string | required in responses | `\\\"\\\"` |\\n\\n**Owner of mutations beyond register defaults:** MARATHON-4 (`PATCH /api/users/me`). This task only sets defaults so envelopes are complete.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C1 — `POST /api/auth/register`\\n\\n| | |\\n|--|--|\\n| Auth | None |\\n| Request body | JSON `{ \\\"username\\\": string, \\\"password\\\": string, \\\"display_name\\\"?: string }` |\\n| Success | `201` `{ \\\"user\\\": UserObj, \\\"token\\\": string }` |\\n| Validation failure | `400` `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` — invalid/missing username, password \\u0026lt; 8, non-object body, wrong types |\\n| Duplicate username | `409` `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` |\\n| Content-Type in | Prefer `application/json`; empty/malformed JSON → `400` |\\n\\n**Server validation (authoritative):**\\n1. Parse JSON object; missing `username` or `password` → `400`.\\n2. `username` must match `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$` → else `400` (e.g. space, hyphen, empty).\\n3. `password` must be string with `.length \\u003e= 8` → else `400`.\\n4. Optional `display_name`: if present and not a string → `400`; if string, trim; empty after trim → treat as omitted (fall back to username).\\n5. Insert user; UNIQUE conflict on case-insensitive username → `409`.\\n6. Create session token; return `201`.\\n\\n**Client (SPA / MARATHON-21) while slow/failing:**\\n- Disable submit / show pending on `auth-submit` until response.\\n- On `201`: store `token` in `localStorage` key `huddle.token`; treat as logged-in; may call `GET /api/auth/me` or use returned `user`.\\n- On `400`/`409`: show `error` string visibly in the auth form (no silent fail).\\n- On network error / 5xx: show generic failure; do not clear unrelated UI state.\\n- **MUST NOT** send an `email` field as required.\\n\\n**Who validates what:** Server is source of truth for slug/password/duplicate. Client may pre-check length for UX but must still handle server `400`/`409`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C2 — `POST /api/auth/login`\\n\\n| | |\\n|--|--|\\n| Auth | None |\\n| Request body | JSON `{ \\\"username\\\": string, \\\"password\\\": string }` |\\n| Success | `200` `{ \\\"user\\\": UserObj, \\\"token\\\": string }` |\\n| Bad credentials | `401` `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` — wrong password **or** unknown username (same code; do not distinguish) |\\n| Malformed body | `400` `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` |\\n\\n**Server:**\\n1. Validate types/presence; malformed → `400`.\\n2. Look up user by case-insensitive username; missing → `401` (same as bad password).\\n3. Verify password with scrypt + stored salt; fail → `401`.\\n4. Issue new token; return `200` with full `UserObj` (current profile fields from DB).\\n\\n**Client:** Same token storage and error surfacing as register. Wrong password must show a visible error, not navigate as success.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C3 — `GET /api/auth/me`\\n\\n| | |\\n|--|--|\\n| Auth | Required: `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` |\\n| Body | None |\\n| Success | `200` `{ \\\"user\\\": UserObj }` |\\n| Missing/invalid/unknown token | `401` `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` |\\n\\n**Header parsing:**\\n- Require header matching `/^Bearer\\\\s+(\\\\S+)$/i` (trim); extract token.\\n- Missing header, wrong scheme, empty token, or token not in DB → `401`.\\n- Do not accept token via query string on this route (query `?token=` is SPA/WS concern later).\\n\\n**Client:** On app load, if `huddle.token` set, call `/api/auth/me`; on `401` clear token and show login; while pending, may show a loading shell without claiming a user.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C4 — Cross-node durability (implicit contract)\\n\\nA user registered or token issued on any of `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` must be accepted by the other two within normal SQLite visibility (immediately after the successful response returns). QA will register on one port and `GET /api/auth/me` on another with the same token.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C5 — Auth middleware seam (internal; for implementers of later tasks)\\n\\n```\\nresolveBearerUser(authorizationHeader: string | null) → UserObj | null\\nrequireUser(req, res) → UserObj | writes 401 and returns null\\n```\\n\\n- Input: raw `Authorization` header value.\\n- Output: public `UserObj` only.\\n- Used by MARATHON-4+, MARATHON-5+, MARATHON-18 (`?token=` maps to same session table), MARATHON-20 (IRC `PASS \\u003ctoken\\u003e`).\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Schema change\\n**New** SQLite DB `/app/data/huddle.db` (greenfield; backward compatible with empty `/app/data/`).\\n\\n#### Table `users`\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `id` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | UUID |\\n| `username` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Original casing |\\n| `username_lower` | TEXT | NOT NULL UNIQUE | `lower(username)` for conflict/login |\\n| `password_salt` | TEXT | NOT NULL | hex or base64 |\\n| `password_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | scrypt output encoding |\\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `'UTC'` | |\\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | RFC3339 UTC |\\n\\n#### Table `tokens`\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `token` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | Opaque bearer (≥16 chars) |\\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `users.id` |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | RFC3339 UTC |\\n\\nIndexes: PK/UNIQUE as above; optional index `tokens(user_id)` for future logout-all (not required this task).\\n\\n**Migrations:** On worker boot, `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` + WAL pragmas. No versioned migration framework required yet; keep DDL in one module (`server/db.js`) so MARATHON-4+ can extend columns carefully.\\n\\n**Password material and salts never appear in HTTP responses.**\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/db.js` | Open `/app/data/huddle.db`, ensure `/app/data` exists, set `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout`, run DDL for `users`/`tokens`, export `getDb()` |\\n| `server/auth/passwords.js` | `hashPassword(password) → {salt, hash}`, `verifyPassword(password, salt, hash) → boolean` using `crypto.scrypt` (sync or promisified consistently) |\\n| `server/auth/tokens.js` | `issueToken(userId) → string` (insert row); `findUserIdByToken(token) → string \\\\| null` |\\n| `server/auth/users.js` | `createUser(...)`, `findUserByUsername(username)`, `publicUser(row) → UserObj` |\\n| `server/auth/middleware.js` | `resolveBearerUser`, `requireUser` |\\n| `server/auth/routes.js` | Handlers for register, login, me; JSON parse helper; status codes per contract |\\n| `server/httpUtil.js` (optional) | `readJson(req)`, `sendJson(res, status, body)` shared with health — only if not already present from MARATHON-2 |\\n\\n### Modify\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/index.js` | Route `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me` before generic 404; keep `GET /api/health` behavior unchanged; initialize DB once at process start (fail boot if DB cannot open) |\\n| `package.json` | No new dependencies required; may note Node ≥22 for `node:sqlite` |\\n| `start.sh` | **No change required** if it already creates `/app/data` (MARATHON-2). If not yet implemented when this lands, ensure `mkdir -p /app/data` remains. Do not move Redis dir. |\\n\\n### Do not modify\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `timer.sh` | Harness timer |\\n| SPA / static HTML | MARATHON-21 |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Within this task\\n1. `db.js` + DDL  \\n2. passwords / users / tokens  \\n3. middleware  \\n4. routes + wire `index.js`  \\n5. Cross-node manual check (register :8000 → me :8001)\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n- Backend implementer owns all files above.\\n- Frontend MARATHON-21 **architecture** can proceed from contracts C1–C3; **implementation** of SPA auth UI should land after (or against mocked) these endpoints.\\n- MARATHON-4 (profiles) extends `users` columns usage and adds routes; must reuse `UserObj` + `requireUser`.\\n- MARATHON-5+ all depend on bearer middleware + durable users.\\n\\n### Seams this task owns\\n| Seam | Downstream |\\n|------|------------|\\n| C1/C2/C3 HTTP auth | MARATHON-21 SPA; QA grader |\\n| `UserObj` shape | MARATHON-4, channel members, messages `author`, WS `user.updated` |\\n| Session table / `resolveBearerUser` | MARATHON-5…20 authenticated APIs; WS `?token=`; IRC `PASS` |\\n| `/app/data/huddle.db` | All durable domain tables (siblings add tables, do not fork a second user DB) |\\n\\n### Build order vs siblings\\n- **Blocked on:** MARATHON-2 bootstrap (ports, `server/index.js`, `/app/data`). If MARATHON-2 is not merged, implementer still codes against its file layout and integrates when bootstrap lands.\\n- **Blocks:** MARATHON-5, MARATHON-11, MARATHON-21 (declared dependents), and practically every authenticated task.\\n\\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\\n| Cut | Owner |\\n|-----|--------|\\n| Profile GET/PATCH + field validation | MARATHON-4 |\\n| Logout / token revoke endpoint | Not in API contract — SPA clears `huddle.token` only; optional later if needed |\\n| WS token query param | MARATHON-18 |\\n| IRC PASS | MARATHON-20 |\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\nNeighborhood scan of architect worktree, `/app`, and repo tree (baseline `timer.sh` only; MARATHON-2 design not yet implemented in tree):\\n\\n| Finding | Why excluded |\\n|---------|----------------|\\n| `timer.sh` | Harness utility |\\n| `GET /api/health` / `start.sh` / Redis | MARATHON-2 |\\n| `GET /api/users/{id}`, `PATCH /api/users/me` | MARATHON-4 |\\n| Workspaces / channels / messages / … | MARATHON-5+ |\\n| SPA auth form, `huddle.token`, testids | MARATHON-21 (consumes C1–C3 only) |\\n| WS `/api/ws?token=` | MARATHON-18 (reuse token table) |\\n| IRC `PASS` / 464 | MARATHON-20 |\\n| Redis pub/sub fan-out | MARATHON-18/19 |\\n| Explicit logout API / token expiry TTL | Not in grader auth contract |\\n| Email verification, OAuth, Slack SDK | Prohibited / not specified |\\n| Rate limiting / CAPTCHA | Not required |\\n\\nNo existing `/api/auth` code or username references in-repo to update.\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| Username `\\\"alice\\\"` then `\\\"Alice\\\"` | Second register → `409` (case-insensitive unique) |\\n| Login with different casing than stored | Succeed if password matches (`username_lower` lookup) |\\n| Password length 7 | `400` on register; login of such user impossible if never created |\\n| Password exactly 8 | Allowed |\\n| `display_name` omitted | `user.display_name === username` |\\n| Extra body fields (`email`, etc.) | Ignore; do not `400` solely for unknown keys |\\n| Duplicate concurrent registers same username | One `201`, other `409` (UNIQUE + handle constraint error) |\\n| SQLite `SQLITE_BUSY` | Retry within `busy_timeout`; if still failing → `500` `{error}` (log stderr); do not corrupt partial user without token |\\n| DB file missing/unwritable at boot | Process exit non-zero; supervisor respawns — fix permissions/`mkdir` in start path |\\n| Token length | Generated tokens always ≥16; reject lookup of empty token as `401` |\\n| `Authorization: bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` | Accept case-insensitive `Bearer` scheme |\\n| `Authorization: Bearer` with no token | `401` |\\n| Method wrong (e.g. `GET /api/auth/register`) | `405` or `404`; must not `500` |\\n| Non-JSON Content-Type with JSON body | Best-effort parse; fail → `400` |\\n| Redis down | Auth **unaffected** (no Redis dependency) |\\n| Node killed mid-request | Client retries; durable commit is atomic per statement/transaction — use a transaction wrapping `INSERT user` + `INSERT token` on register so a crash does not leave user without usable session or orphan inconsistently (prefer: commit user first then token; if token insert fails after user commit, return `500` and allow login to mint a token) |\\n| Register success transaction | Prefer single transaction: insert user + insert token; on success return `201` |\\n| `/api/auth/me` with valid token after profile defaults | Returns current DB fields (same shape MARATHON-4 will later mutate) |\\n| Leading/trailing spaces in username | **Reject** (`400`) — must match regex exactly; do not auto-trim to accept `\\\" alice\\\"` |\\n| Unicode passwords | Allowed; length is JS string length ≥ 8 |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `POST /api/auth/register` with valid `{username,password}` → `201`, body has `user` and `token`, `token.length \\u003e= 16`, `user` includes all seven `UserObj` fields.\\n2. Same username again (any casing) → `409` with JSON `error`.\\n3. Username containing a space (or hyphen/other special) → `400`.\\n4. Password length 7 → `400`.\\n5. No `email` required: body without email succeeds when username/password valid.\\n6. `POST /api/auth/login` with correct credentials → `200` `{user,token}`; new token usable on `/me`.\\n7. Wrong password → `401`; unknown username → `401` (not `404`).\\n8. `GET /api/auth/me` with `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` → `200` `{user}` matching the registered user id/username.\\n9. Missing header, garbage token, or malformed Authorization → `401`.\\n10. Register on `127.0.0.1:8000`, then `GET /api/auth/me` on `:8001` and `:8002` with the same token → `200` (shared durable store).\\n11. Kill Redis; register/login/me still succeed on any node.\\n12. **MUST NOT:** put `password`, `password_hash`, or `password_salt` in any response body.\\n13. **MUST NOT:** change `GET /api/health` semantics or port/`node_id` mapping.\\n14. Responses use `Content-Type: application/json` (charset utf-8 preferred).\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Scripted (implementer / QA)\\n```bash\\n# assume cluster up via start.sh\\ncurl -sS -D- -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/register \\\\\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"username\\\":\\\"alice\\\",\\\"password\\\":\\\"password1\\\"}'\\n# expect 201; capture token\\ncurl -sS -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\\\" http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/auth/me\\n# expect 200 same user\\ncurl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8002/api/auth/login \\\\\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"username\\\":\\\"Alice\\\",\\\"password\\\":\\\"password1\\\"}'\\n# negative cases: short password, space username, dup, bad login, me without token\\n```\\n\\n### Scenarios that matter\\n- Cross-node token acceptance (criterion 10).\\n- Case-insensitive duplicate + case-insensitive login.\\n- Redis-down auth still works.\\n- Concurrent double-register race → one 201 one 409.\\n\\n### Manual human verification\\nBoot cluster, run the curls above against all three ports, confirm `/app/data/huddle.db` exists and contains rows (`sqlite3 /app/data/huddle.db 'SELECT username FROM users;'`). Confirm health still ok during auth tests.\\n\\n### Out of scope for this task’s tests\\nSPA form, logout UI, profile PATCH, workspace creation, WS/IRC token use.\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"New design (no needs-revision). Auth + shared SQLite at /app/data/huddle.db via node:sqlite; Redis not used for durability. Aligns with MARATHON-2 conventions. After lead removes architect label, implementer is backend (label already present). SPA MARATHON-21 consumes C1–C3 only.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:28:48.996953698Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:35:03.653744462Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"Implement POST /api/auth/register, POST /api/auth/login, GET /api/auth/me per API contract. Username slug rules, password \\u003e=8, 201/200 envelopes {user,token} or {user}, 400/401/409 as specified. Token length \\u003e=16. Shared durable store across all three nodes.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-5\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-3\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Workspaces: create, list, detail, members, roles, ownership\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:28:56.937950024Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-11\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-3\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Files: upload, metadata, download, attach to messages\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:29:08.879491643Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-21\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-3\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA shell: auth UI, token storage, logout/login\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:29:38.147739939Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help            help for data\n  -o, --output string   Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string   Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n\nUse \"loom data [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-22T19:35:33.594Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\n","executionTime":393,"interleavedOutput":"Already up to date.\ntime=2026-08-22T19:35:33.594Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-3\",\n  \"title\": \"Auth: register, login, me, bearer tokens\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"priority\": 0,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"assignee\": \"frontend-dev-1\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"backend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"## Summary\\n\\nMARATHON-3 implements cluster-wide authentication for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, plus the shared durable user/token store that all three HTTP nodes read and write. It establishes the `UserObj` identity shape, opaque bearer tokens (`Authorization: Bearer …`), password hashing, username slug validation, and a reusable auth middleware that every later authenticated route (workspaces, channels, WS, IRC `PASS`, SPA) will call. Without this seam, no other feature can attribute callers or survive a request to a different node.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n- **Runtime:** Stay on the MARATHON-2 stack: Node.js stdlib `http` router in `server/index.js`, no Express/Fastify required.\\n- **Durable shared store:** One **SQLite** database file at `/app/data/huddle.db`, opened by each HTTP worker via Node’s built-in **`node:sqlite` (`DatabaseSync`)**. Enable **WAL** + a non-zero `busy_timeout` so concurrent register/login from nodes 0/1/2 serialize safely. This is the authoritative store for users and sessions; **Redis is not used for auth durability** (Redis may be killed; users/tokens must survive).\\n- **Passwords:** `crypto.scrypt` with a per-user random salt; store only `password_salt` + `password_hash` (never plaintext). Compare with timing-safe equality.\\n- **Tokens:** Opaque random strings from `crypto.randomBytes` (≥16 chars when encoded; generate **32 bytes → base64url ≈ 43 chars**). Persist token → `user_id` in SQLite. Each successful register/login **issues a new token** (multiple concurrent sessions allowed). Tokens are looked up as presented; no JWT.\\n- **IDs:** Stable cluster-wide `user.id` via `crypto.randomUUID()` (string UUID).\\n- **Auth helper:** Export `authenticateRequest(req) → user | null` and/or middleware used by `/api/auth/me` and reserved for MARATHON-4+.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\\n|-------------|--------------|\\n| Redis HASH for users/tokens | Not durable across Redis SIGKILL; epic requires cluster to keep working when Redis dies |\\n| Per-node in-memory maps | Breaks “shared durable store across all three nodes”; register on :8000 would 401 on :8001 |\\n| JWT without server-side session | Harder to revoke; contract only needs opaque bearer length ≥16; SQLite session rows are simpler and match IRC/WS token checks later |\\n| npm `better-sqlite3` / Express | Unnecessary dependency; `node:sqlite` is available on Node 24 in this environment |\\n| JSON file + flock only | Workable but weaker concurrency and no unique indexes for username race → prefer SQLite UNIQUE |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\nSQLite file locking under three processes is simpler than a real DB server, but write throughput under heavy concurrent register is limited by WAL/busy waits. Acceptable for marathon scale. Using experimental `node:sqlite` avoids npm install in air-gapped/self-contained constraints; if the API shifts, implementer may pin Node flags or swap to an equivalent sync SQLite binding **without changing the HTTP contract**.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited from MARATHON-2 (authoritative)\\n| Convention | Value |\\n|------------|--------|\\n| App root | `/app` |\\n| HTTP entry | `server/index.js`, `NODE_ID` / `PORT` |\\n| Durable root | `/app/data/` |\\n| API prefix | `/api/...` |\\n| JSON | `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8` |\\n| Health | Unchanged; still Redis-independent |\\n\\n### Conventions fixed here (for siblings)\\n| Convention | Value |\\n|------------|--------|\\n| DB path | `/app/data/huddle.db` (create parent dir if missing) |\\n| `UserObj` public fields | `{id, username, display_name, timezone, avatar_url, status_text, status_emoji}` — always present on auth responses |\\n| Username rules | Regex `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$` (letters, digits, underscore only; no spaces/hyphens/dots) |\\n| Username uniqueness | Case-insensitive (`LOWER(username)` UNIQUE); store username with original casing from register |\\n| Password | UTF-8 string length ≥ 8 (code units / JS `.length`); no other complexity rules |\\n| Bearer | Header `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` (single space); token string length ≥ 16 |\\n| Error JSON | `{ \\\"error\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\" }` for 400/401/409 (message text open; must be non-empty) |\\n| No email | Register/login bodies must not require `email`; ignore unknown fields |\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Shared: `UserObj` (public; never include password/hash/salt/token)\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"\\u003cuuid-string\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"username\\\": \\\"\\u003cslug\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"display_name\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"timezone\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"avatar_url\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"status_text\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\",\\n  \\\"status_emoji\\\": \\\"\\u003cstring\\u003e\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n| Field | Type | Nullability | Default on register |\\n|-------|------|-------------|---------------------|\\n| `id` | string (UUID) | required | generated |\\n| `username` | string | required | from body |\\n| `display_name` | string | required in responses | `display_name` if provided non-empty, else copy of `username` |\\n| `timezone` | string | required in responses | `\\\"UTC\\\"` |\\n| `avatar_url` | string | required in responses | `\\\"\\\"` |\\n| `status_text` | string | required in responses | `\\\"\\\"` |\\n| `status_emoji` | string | required in responses | `\\\"\\\"` |\\n\\n**Owner of mutations beyond register defaults:** MARATHON-4 (`PATCH /api/users/me`). This task only sets defaults so envelopes are complete.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C1 — `POST /api/auth/register`\\n\\n| | |\\n|--|--|\\n| Auth | None |\\n| Request body | JSON `{ \\\"username\\\": string, \\\"password\\\": string, \\\"display_name\\\"?: string }` |\\n| Success | `201` `{ \\\"user\\\": UserObj, \\\"token\\\": string }` |\\n| Validation failure | `400` `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` — invalid/missing username, password \\u0026lt; 8, non-object body, wrong types |\\n| Duplicate username | `409` `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` |\\n| Content-Type in | Prefer `application/json`; empty/malformed JSON → `400` |\\n\\n**Server validation (authoritative):**\\n1. Parse JSON object; missing `username` or `password` → `400`.\\n2. `username` must match `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$` → else `400` (e.g. space, hyphen, empty).\\n3. `password` must be string with `.length \\u003e= 8` → else `400`.\\n4. Optional `display_name`: if present and not a string → `400`; if string, trim; empty after trim → treat as omitted (fall back to username).\\n5. Insert user; UNIQUE conflict on case-insensitive username → `409`.\\n6. Create session token; return `201`.\\n\\n**Client (SPA / MARATHON-21) while slow/failing:**\\n- Disable submit / show pending on `auth-submit` until response.\\n- On `201`: store `token` in `localStorage` key `huddle.token`; treat as logged-in; may call `GET /api/auth/me` or use returned `user`.\\n- On `400`/`409`: show `error` string visibly in the auth form (no silent fail).\\n- On network error / 5xx: show generic failure; do not clear unrelated UI state.\\n- **MUST NOT** send an `email` field as required.\\n\\n**Who validates what:** Server is source of truth for slug/password/duplicate. Client may pre-check length for UX but must still handle server `400`/`409`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C2 — `POST /api/auth/login`\\n\\n| | |\\n|--|--|\\n| Auth | None |\\n| Request body | JSON `{ \\\"username\\\": string, \\\"password\\\": string }` |\\n| Success | `200` `{ \\\"user\\\": UserObj, \\\"token\\\": string }` |\\n| Bad credentials | `401` `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` — wrong password **or** unknown username (same code; do not distinguish) |\\n| Malformed body | `400` `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` |\\n\\n**Server:**\\n1. Validate types/presence; malformed → `400`.\\n2. Look up user by case-insensitive username; missing → `401` (same as bad password).\\n3. Verify password with scrypt + stored salt; fail → `401`.\\n4. Issue new token; return `200` with full `UserObj` (current profile fields from DB).\\n\\n**Client:** Same token storage and error surfacing as register. Wrong password must show a visible error, not navigate as success.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C3 — `GET /api/auth/me`\\n\\n| | |\\n|--|--|\\n| Auth | Required: `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` |\\n| Body | None |\\n| Success | `200` `{ \\\"user\\\": UserObj }` |\\n| Missing/invalid/unknown token | `401` `{ \\\"error\\\": string }` |\\n\\n**Header parsing:**\\n- Require header matching `/^Bearer\\\\s+(\\\\S+)$/i` (trim); extract token.\\n- Missing header, wrong scheme, empty token, or token not in DB → `401`.\\n- Do not accept token via query string on this route (query `?token=` is SPA/WS concern later).\\n\\n**Client:** On app load, if `huddle.token` set, call `/api/auth/me`; on `401` clear token and show login; while pending, may show a loading shell without claiming a user.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C4 — Cross-node durability (implicit contract)\\n\\nA user registered or token issued on any of `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` must be accepted by the other two within normal SQLite visibility (immediately after the successful response returns). QA will register on one port and `GET /api/auth/me` on another with the same token.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C5 — Auth middleware seam (internal; for implementers of later tasks)\\n\\n```\\nresolveBearerUser(authorizationHeader: string | null) → UserObj | null\\nrequireUser(req, res) → UserObj | writes 401 and returns null\\n```\\n\\n- Input: raw `Authorization` header value.\\n- Output: public `UserObj` only.\\n- Used by MARATHON-4+, MARATHON-5+, MARATHON-18 (`?token=` maps to same session table), MARATHON-20 (IRC `PASS \\u003ctoken\\u003e`).\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Schema change\\n**New** SQLite DB `/app/data/huddle.db` (greenfield; backward compatible with empty `/app/data/`).\\n\\n#### Table `users`\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `id` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | UUID |\\n| `username` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Original casing |\\n| `username_lower` | TEXT | NOT NULL UNIQUE | `lower(username)` for conflict/login |\\n| `password_salt` | TEXT | NOT NULL | hex or base64 |\\n| `password_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | scrypt output encoding |\\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `'UTC'` | |\\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | RFC3339 UTC |\\n\\n#### Table `tokens`\\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\\n|--------|------|------|-------|\\n| `token` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | Opaque bearer (≥16 chars) |\\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `users.id` |\\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | RFC3339 UTC |\\n\\nIndexes: PK/UNIQUE as above; optional index `tokens(user_id)` for future logout-all (not required this task).\\n\\n**Migrations:** On worker boot, `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` + WAL pragmas. No versioned migration framework required yet; keep DDL in one module (`server/db.js`) so MARATHON-4+ can extend columns carefully.\\n\\n**Password material and salts never appear in HTTP responses.**\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/db.js` | Open `/app/data/huddle.db`, ensure `/app/data` exists, set `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout`, run DDL for `users`/`tokens`, export `getDb()` |\\n| `server/auth/passwords.js` | `hashPassword(password) → {salt, hash}`, `verifyPassword(password, salt, hash) → boolean` using `crypto.scrypt` (sync or promisified consistently) |\\n| `server/auth/tokens.js` | `issueToken(userId) → string` (insert row); `findUserIdByToken(token) → string \\\\| null` |\\n| `server/auth/users.js` | `createUser(...)`, `findUserByUsername(username)`, `publicUser(row) → UserObj` |\\n| `server/auth/middleware.js` | `resolveBearerUser`, `requireUser` |\\n| `server/auth/routes.js` | Handlers for register, login, me; JSON parse helper; status codes per contract |\\n| `server/httpUtil.js` (optional) | `readJson(req)`, `sendJson(res, status, body)` shared with health — only if not already present from MARATHON-2 |\\n\\n### Modify\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/index.js` | Route `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me` before generic 404; keep `GET /api/health` behavior unchanged; initialize DB once at process start (fail boot if DB cannot open) |\\n| `package.json` | No new dependencies required; may note Node ≥22 for `node:sqlite` |\\n| `start.sh` | **No change required** if it already creates `/app/data` (MARATHON-2). If not yet implemented when this lands, ensure `mkdir -p /app/data` remains. Do not move Redis dir. |\\n\\n### Do not modify\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `timer.sh` | Harness timer |\\n| SPA / static HTML | MARATHON-21 |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Within this task\\n1. `db.js` + DDL  \\n2. passwords / users / tokens  \\n3. middleware  \\n4. routes + wire `index.js`  \\n5. Cross-node manual check (register :8000 → me :8001)\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n- Backend implementer owns all files above.\\n- Frontend MARATHON-21 **architecture** can proceed from contracts C1–C3; **implementation** of SPA auth UI should land after (or against mocked) these endpoints.\\n- MARATHON-4 (profiles) extends `users` columns usage and adds routes; must reuse `UserObj` + `requireUser`.\\n- MARATHON-5+ all depend on bearer middleware + durable users.\\n\\n### Seams this task owns\\n| Seam | Downstream |\\n|------|------------|\\n| C1/C2/C3 HTTP auth | MARATHON-21 SPA; QA grader |\\n| `UserObj` shape | MARATHON-4, channel members, messages `author`, WS `user.updated` |\\n| Session table / `resolveBearerUser` | MARATHON-5…20 authenticated APIs; WS `?token=`; IRC `PASS` |\\n| `/app/data/huddle.db` | All durable domain tables (siblings add tables, do not fork a second user DB) |\\n\\n### Build order vs siblings\\n- **Blocked on:** MARATHON-2 bootstrap (ports, `server/index.js`, `/app/data`). If MARATHON-2 is not merged, implementer still codes against its file layout and integrates when bootstrap lands.\\n- **Blocks:** MARATHON-5, MARATHON-11, MARATHON-21 (declared dependents), and practically every authenticated task.\\n\\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\\n| Cut | Owner |\\n|-----|--------|\\n| Profile GET/PATCH + field validation | MARATHON-4 |\\n| Logout / token revoke endpoint | Not in API contract — SPA clears `huddle.token` only; optional later if needed |\\n| WS token query param | MARATHON-18 |\\n| IRC PASS | MARATHON-20 |\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\nNeighborhood scan of architect worktree, `/app`, and repo tree (baseline `timer.sh` only; MARATHON-2 design not yet implemented in tree):\\n\\n| Finding | Why excluded |\\n|---------|----------------|\\n| `timer.sh` | Harness utility |\\n| `GET /api/health` / `start.sh` / Redis | MARATHON-2 |\\n| `GET /api/users/{id}`, `PATCH /api/users/me` | MARATHON-4 |\\n| Workspaces / channels / messages / … | MARATHON-5+ |\\n| SPA auth form, `huddle.token`, testids | MARATHON-21 (consumes C1–C3 only) |\\n| WS `/api/ws?token=` | MARATHON-18 (reuse token table) |\\n| IRC `PASS` / 464 | MARATHON-20 |\\n| Redis pub/sub fan-out | MARATHON-18/19 |\\n| Explicit logout API / token expiry TTL | Not in grader auth contract |\\n| Email verification, OAuth, Slack SDK | Prohibited / not specified |\\n| Rate limiting / CAPTCHA | Not required |\\n\\nNo existing `/api/auth` code or username references in-repo to update.\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\\n|-----------|-------------------|\\n| Username `\\\"alice\\\"` then `\\\"Alice\\\"` | Second register → `409` (case-insensitive unique) |\\n| Login with different casing than stored | Succeed if password matches (`username_lower` lookup) |\\n| Password length 7 | `400` on register; login of such user impossible if never created |\\n| Password exactly 8 | Allowed |\\n| `display_name` omitted | `user.display_name === username` |\\n| Extra body fields (`email`, etc.) | Ignore; do not `400` solely for unknown keys |\\n| Duplicate concurrent registers same username | One `201`, other `409` (UNIQUE + handle constraint error) |\\n| SQLite `SQLITE_BUSY` | Retry within `busy_timeout`; if still failing → `500` `{error}` (log stderr); do not corrupt partial user without token |\\n| DB file missing/unwritable at boot | Process exit non-zero; supervisor respawns — fix permissions/`mkdir` in start path |\\n| Token length | Generated tokens always ≥16; reject lookup of empty token as `401` |\\n| `Authorization: bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` | Accept case-insensitive `Bearer` scheme |\\n| `Authorization: Bearer` with no token | `401` |\\n| Method wrong (e.g. `GET /api/auth/register`) | `405` or `404`; must not `500` |\\n| Non-JSON Content-Type with JSON body | Best-effort parse; fail → `400` |\\n| Redis down | Auth **unaffected** (no Redis dependency) |\\n| Node killed mid-request | Client retries; durable commit is atomic per statement/transaction — use a transaction wrapping `INSERT user` + `INSERT token` on register so a crash does not leave user without usable session or orphan inconsistently (prefer: commit user first then token; if token insert fails after user commit, return `500` and allow login to mint a token) |\\n| Register success transaction | Prefer single transaction: insert user + insert token; on success return `201` |\\n| `/api/auth/me` with valid token after profile defaults | Returns current DB fields (same shape MARATHON-4 will later mutate) |\\n| Leading/trailing spaces in username | **Reject** (`400`) — must match regex exactly; do not auto-trim to accept `\\\" alice\\\"` |\\n| Unicode passwords | Allowed; length is JS string length ≥ 8 |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `POST /api/auth/register` with valid `{username,password}` → `201`, body has `user` and `token`, `token.length \\u003e= 16`, `user` includes all seven `UserObj` fields.\\n2. Same username again (any casing) → `409` with JSON `error`.\\n3. Username containing a space (or hyphen/other special) → `400`.\\n4. Password length 7 → `400`.\\n5. No `email` required: body without email succeeds when username/password valid.\\n6. `POST /api/auth/login` with correct credentials → `200` `{user,token}`; new token usable on `/me`.\\n7. Wrong password → `401`; unknown username → `401` (not `404`).\\n8. `GET /api/auth/me` with `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` → `200` `{user}` matching the registered user id/username.\\n9. Missing header, garbage token, or malformed Authorization → `401`.\\n10. Register on `127.0.0.1:8000`, then `GET /api/auth/me` on `:8001` and `:8002` with the same token → `200` (shared durable store).\\n11. Kill Redis; register/login/me still succeed on any node.\\n12. **MUST NOT:** put `password`, `password_hash`, or `password_salt` in any response body.\\n13. **MUST NOT:** change `GET /api/health` semantics or port/`node_id` mapping.\\n14. Responses use `Content-Type: application/json` (charset utf-8 preferred).\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Scripted (implementer / QA)\\n```bash\\n# assume cluster up via start.sh\\ncurl -sS -D- -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/register \\\\\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"username\\\":\\\"alice\\\",\\\"password\\\":\\\"password1\\\"}'\\n# expect 201; capture token\\ncurl -sS -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\\\" http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/auth/me\\n# expect 200 same user\\ncurl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8002/api/auth/login \\\\\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"username\\\":\\\"Alice\\\",\\\"password\\\":\\\"password1\\\"}'\\n# negative cases: short password, space username, dup, bad login, me without token\\n```\\n\\n### Scenarios that matter\\n- Cross-node token acceptance (criterion 10).\\n- Case-insensitive duplicate + case-insensitive login.\\n- Redis-down auth still works.\\n- Concurrent double-register race → one 201 one 409.\\n\\n### Manual human verification\\nBoot cluster, run the curls above against all three ports, confirm `/app/data/huddle.db` exists and contains rows (`sqlite3 /app/data/huddle.db 'SELECT username FROM users;'`). Confirm health still ok during auth tests.\\n\\n### Out of scope for this task’s tests\\nSPA form, logout UI, profile PATCH, workspace creation, WS/IRC token use.\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"New design (no needs-revision). Auth + shared SQLite at /app/data/huddle.db via node:sqlite; Redis not used for durability. Aligns with MARATHON-2 conventions. After lead removes architect label, implementer is backend (label already present). SPA MARATHON-21 consumes C1–C3 only.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:28:48.996953698Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:35:03.653744462Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"Implement POST /api/auth/register, POST /api/auth/login, GET /api/auth/me per API contract. Username slug rules, password \\u003e=8, 201/200 envelopes {user,token} or {user}, 400/401/409 as specified. Token length \\u003e=16. Shared durable store across all three nodes.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-5\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-3\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Workspaces: create, list, detail, members, roles, ownership\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:28:56.937950024Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-11\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-3\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"Files: upload, metadata, download, attach to messages\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:29:08.879491643Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-21\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-3\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA shell: auth UI, token storage, logout/login\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T19:29:38.147739939Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help            help for data\n  -o, --output string   Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string   Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n\nUse \"loom data [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","localExecutionTimeMs":67},"isBackground":false},"description":"Merge main and show task JSON"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-fb623cb8-56c7-4905-9ab3-e178a9b2511c-0\nfc_a2d0c02a-0cd3-9a38-a460-c904f3a98e5c_0","startedAtMs":"1787427333233","completedAtMs":"1787427333626"},"model_call_id":"2a37d5f9-56a3-4465-9a86-d97d098d1dd3-0-cjdd","session_id":"b8e62675-1c0a-43a6-b50e-0b06cb55e7dc","timestamp_ms":1787427333673}
