{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-1d75feb6-7046-4c1f-9eb9-7a9c72fbcd91-7\nfc_e5e7c324-fc01-972e-a3d1-73a11bacabe2_1","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-2 --output json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint(d.get('design') or '')\n\" > /tmp/m2-design.md && rg -n \"File|server/|start\\.sh|Component|inventory|NODE_ID|Acceptance\" /tmp/m2-design.md | head -60; echo '---'; head -100 /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/server/index.js; echo '---'; cat /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/package.json; echo '---'; head -80 /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/start.sh","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-1d75feb6-7046-4c1f-9eb9-7a9c72fbcd91-7\nfc_e5e7c324-fc01-972e-a3d1-73a11bacabe2_1","simpleCommands":["loom","python3","rg","head","echo","head","echo","cat","echo","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-2"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-2 --output json"},{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"string","value":"\"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint(d.get('design') or '')\n\""}],"fullText":"python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint(d.get('design') or '')\n\""},{"name":"rg","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-n"},{"type":"string","value":"\"File|server/|start\\.sh|Component|inventory|NODE_ID|Acceptance\""},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/m2-design.md"}],"fullText":"rg -n \"File|server/|start\\.sh|Component|inventory|NODE_ID|Acceptance\" /tmp/m2-design.md"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-60"}],"fullText":"head -60"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---'"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-100"},{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/server/index.js"}],"fullText":"head -100 /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/server/index.js"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---'"},{"name":"cat","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/package.json"}],"fullText":"cat /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/package.json"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"raw_string","value":"'---'"}],"fullText":"echo '---'"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-80"},{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/start.sh"}],"fullText":"head -80 /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/start.sh"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/m2-design.md"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Read M2 design and sibling WIP server","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"b8e62675-1c0a-43a6-b50e-0b06cb55e7dc","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-2 --output json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint(d.get('design') or '')\n\" > /tmp/m2-design.md && rg -n \"File|server/|start\\.sh|Component|inventory|NODE_ID|Acceptance\" /tmp/m2-design.md | head -60; echo '---'; head -100 /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/server/index.js; echo '---'; cat /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/package.json; echo '---'; head -80 /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/start.sh","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"3:MARATHON-2 bootstraps the Huddle cluster runtime at `/app`: a foreground `start.sh` that launches local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, keeps them alive under SIGKILL (HTTP respawn ≤60s; Redis respawn after kill), and exposes a stable `GET /api/health` contract returning `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` with `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` matching ports. This is the foundation every later auth, messaging, WS, IRC, and SPA task assumes: process topology, port map, node identity, and local-only Redis.\n8:- **Process model:** One bash supervisor (`/app/start.sh`) stays in the foreground and owns child lifetimes. Children: one `redis-server` + three Node.js HTTP workers. The supervisor polls PIDs (≈1s cadence) and respawns any dead child without exiting.\n9:- **HTTP runtime:** **Node.js** (v24 present in the environment) using the **stdlib `http` module only** for this task—no npm registry dependency for bootstrap. One shared entrypoint, differentiated solely by `NODE_ID` / `PORT` env vars.\n10:- **Redis:** System `redis-server` (v7 present), bound to `127.0.0.1:6379`, persistence directory under `/app/data/redis`. Started as a non-daemon child of `start.sh` (no `--daemonize yes`) so the supervisor can track its PID.\n18:| Three separate start scripts | Harness expects a single foreground `/app/start.sh` |\n22:Supervisor simplicity (bash PID loop) over a real process manager: enough for marathon verification (kill + respawn windows), but no fancy backoff/jitter. Fixed ports mean `start.sh` must fail loudly if a protected harness process already owns a port rather than silently remapping.\n31:| HTTP runtime | Node.js, CommonJS or ESM; entry `server/index.js` |\n32:| Node identity | Integer `NODE_ID` ∈ {0,1,2}; `PORT = 8000 + NODE_ID` |\n34:| Durable shared state | Files under `/app/data/` (schema owned by MARATHON-3+; this task only creates dirs) |\n64:- Server: derives `node_id` only from its configured `NODE_ID` env (integer parse once at boot); does not trust client input.\n72:| HTTP node 0 | `127.0.0.1:8000` | `NODE_ID=0` |\n73:| HTTP node 1 | `127.0.0.1:8001` | `NODE_ID=1` |\n74:| HTTP node 2 | `127.0.0.1:8002` | `NODE_ID=2` |\n76:`start.sh` remains in the foreground until terminated by signal; killing an HTTP child or Redis must not stop the supervisor or the other children.\n89:| `NODE_ID` | integer 0\\|1\\|2 | yes (HTTP workers) | Stable node identity in health + future logs |\n90:| `PORT` | integer | yes (HTTP workers) | Listen port; must equal `8000 + NODE_ID` |\n94:**On-disk (created by `start.sh` if missing):**\n103:## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n106:| File | Change |\n108:| `/app/start.sh` | Executable foreground supervisor: prepare dirs, spawn Redis + 3 nodes, trap signals, poll/respawn loop, log to stdout/stderr |\n109:| `/app/server/index.js` | HTTP server entry: read `NODE_ID`/`PORT`, bind `127.0.0.1:$PORT`, route `GET /api/health`, reject invalid env at boot with non-zero exit |\n110:| `/app/server/health.js` | Pure handler building `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` (keeps routing thin for later middleware) |\n111:| `/app/package.json` | `{ \"name\": \"huddle\", \"private\": true, \"main\": \"server/index.js\" }` — documents Node entry; **no required dependencies** for this task |\n114:| File | Change |\n119:| File | Change |\n126:1. `server/health.js` + `server/index.js` (can be verified with a one-off `NODE_ID=0 PORT=8000 node server/index.js` by the implementer—architect does not run the app).\n128:3. `start.sh` (depends on server entry existing)\n129:4. Manual/QA: boot via `start.sh`, hit three health URLs, kill tests\n141:| Foreground `start.sh` | stays up, respawns | Harness lifecycle; MARATHON-19/20 extend children later |\n150:| IRC `:6667` process under same supervisor | MARATHON-20 (will extend `start.sh` to launch IRC gateway + respawn) |\n153:When MARATHON-20/21 land, they **extend** `start.sh` and the HTTP router; they must not replace the health contract or port map.\n172:No prior `start.sh`, `/api/health`, or `node_id` references exist in-repo to update.\n178:| `NODE_ID` missing or not in `{0,1,2}` | Worker prints error to stderr and exits non-zero; supervisor respawns—**implementer must pass valid env from `start.sh` so this is a programming error, not a loop** |\n179:| `PORT` missing or ≠ `8000+NODE_ID` | Same: fail fast at worker boot |\n181:| Redis already running on 6379 (foreign process) | `redis-server` fails; supervisor respawns Redis child. Log bind failure. Do not kill arbitrary PIDs outside children started by this `start.sh` (harness `marathon-freeports` is for verifiers, not the app). |\n184:| `start.sh` receives SIGINT/SIGTERM | Trap: stop respawn loop, signal/kill tracked children, then exit non-zero or 0 per convention (prefer 0 on clean TERM); do not leave orphaned node/redis children |\n188:| Double-start of `start.sh` | Second instance will fail binds; document that only one supervisor should run. No distributed lock required for marathon |\n189:| Working directory | `start.sh` `cd`s to its own directory (`/app`) so relative paths work regardless of caller cwd |\n192:## Acceptance Criteria\n194:1. Running `/app/start.sh` does not daemonize away: the script process remains in the foreground and continues until signaled.\n202:9. **MUST NOT:** remap ports; change `node_id` mapping; require Redis up for health; exit `start.sh` when a single child dies.\n207:- Boot: `/app/start.sh` in background job **only for the test harness** (script itself still runs as a foreground process in that job).\n212:- Tear down via SIGTERM to `start.sh`; confirm ports free (or document leftover only if trap failed—trap must succeed).\n216:/app/start.sh\n---\n'use strict';\n\nconst http = require('http');\nconst { sendHealth } = require('./health');\n\nfunction parseEnv() {\n  const rawId = process.env.NODE_ID;\n  const rawPort = process.env.PORT;\n\n  if (rawId === undefined || rawId === '') {\n    console.error('NODE_ID is required (0, 1, or 2)');\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const nodeId = Number(rawId);\n  if (!Number.isInteger(nodeId) || nodeId < 0 || nodeId > 2) {\n    console.error(`Invalid NODE_ID: ${rawId} (must be integer 0, 1, or 2)`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  if (rawPort === undefined || rawPort === '') {\n    console.error('PORT is required');\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const port = Number(rawPort);\n  const expected = 8000 + nodeId;\n  if (!Number.isInteger(port) || port !== expected) {\n    console.error(`PORT must equal 8000+NODE_ID (${expected}), got: ${rawPort}`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  return { nodeId, port };\n}\n\nconst { nodeId, port } = parseEnv();\n\nconst server = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n  let pathname = '/';\n  try {\n    pathname = new URL(req.url || '/', `http://127.0.0.1:${port}`).pathname;\n  } catch {\n    pathname = '/';\n  }\n\n  if (pathname === '/api/health') {\n    if (req.method === 'GET') {\n      sendHealth(res, nodeId);\n      return;\n    }\n    const body = JSON.stringify({ error: 'method_not_allowed' });\n    res.writeHead(405, {\n      'Content-Type': 'application/json; charset=utf-8',\n      'Content-Length': Buffer.byteLength(body),\n    });\n    res.end(body);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const body = JSON.stringify({ error: 'not_found' });\n  res.writeHead(404, {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json; charset=utf-8',\n    'Content-Length': Buffer.byteLength(body),\n  });\n  res.end(body);\n});\n\nserver.on('error', (err) => {\n  console.error(`[node-${nodeId}] Failed to bind 127.0.0.1:${port}: ${err.message}`);\n  process.exit(1);\n});\n\nserver.listen(port, '127.0.0.1', () => {\n  console.error(`[node-${nodeId}] listening on 127.0.0.1:${port}`);\n});\n---\n{\n  \"name\": \"huddle\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"main\": \"server/index.js\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"node --test test/*.test.js\"\n  }\n}\n---\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Huddle cluster supervisor: Redis + three HTTP nodes. Stays in the foreground.\nset -u\n\nAPP_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\ncd \"$APP_DIR\" || exit 1\n\nNODE_BIN=\"${NODE_BIN:-}\"\nif [[ -z \"$NODE_BIN\" ]]; then\n  if [[ -x /usr/bin/node ]]; then\n    NODE_BIN=/usr/bin/node\n  else\n    NODE_BIN=\"$(command -v node || true)\"\n  fi\nfi\nif [[ -z \"$NODE_BIN\" || ! -x \"$NODE_BIN\" ]]; then\n  echo \"[supervisor] node binary not found\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nREDIS_BIN=\"$(command -v redis-server || true)\"\nif [[ -z \"$REDIS_BIN\" ]]; then\n  echo \"[supervisor] redis-server not found\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nmkdir -p \"$APP_DIR/data/redis\"\n\nREDIS_PID=\"\"\ndeclare -a NODE_PIDS=(\"\" \"\" \"\")\nSHUTTING_DOWN=0\n\nprefix_stream() {\n  local prefix=\"$1\"\n  while IFS= read -r line || [[ -n \"${line:-}\" ]]; do\n    printf '%s %s\\n' \"$prefix\" \"$line\"\n  done\n}\n\nis_alive() {\n  local pid=\"${1:-}\"\n  [[ -n \"$pid\" ]] && kill -0 \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null\n}\n\nstart_redis() {\n  if [[ -f \"$APP_DIR/redis.conf\" ]]; then\n    \"$REDIS_BIN\" \"$APP_DIR/redis.conf\" \\\n      > >(prefix_stream '[redis]') 2>&1 &\n  else\n    \"$REDIS_BIN\" \\\n      --bind 127.0.0.1 \\\n      --port 6379 \\\n      --dir \"$APP_DIR/data/redis\" \\\n      --protected-mode yes \\\n      --daemonize no \\\n      --save \"\" \\\n      --appendonly no \\\n      > >(prefix_stream '[redis]') 2>&1 &\n  fi\n  REDIS_PID=$!\n  echo \"[supervisor] started redis pid=$REDIS_PID\"\n}\n\nstart_node() {\n  local id=\"$1\"\n  local port=$((8000 + id))\n  NODE_ID=\"$id\" PORT=\"$port\" \"$NODE_BIN\" \"$APP_DIR/server/index.js\" \\\n    > >(prefix_stream \"[node-$id]\") 2>&1 &\n  NODE_PIDS[$id]=$!\n  echo \"[supervisor] started node-$id pid=${NODE_PIDS[$id]} port=$port\"\n}\n\nstop_children() {\n  local pid\n  for pid in \"${NODE_PIDS[@]:-}\" \"$REDIS_PID\"; do\n    if is_alive \"$pid\"; then\n      kill \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\n    fi\n  done\n  sleep 0.2\n","stderr":"","executionTime":116,"interleavedOutput":"3:MARATHON-2 bootstraps the Huddle cluster runtime at `/app`: a foreground `start.sh` that launches local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, keeps them alive under SIGKILL (HTTP respawn ≤60s; Redis respawn after kill), and exposes a stable `GET /api/health` contract returning `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` with `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` matching ports. This is the foundation every later auth, messaging, WS, IRC, and SPA task assumes: process topology, port map, node identity, and local-only Redis.\n8:- **Process model:** One bash supervisor (`/app/start.sh`) stays in the foreground and owns child lifetimes. Children: one `redis-server` + three Node.js HTTP workers. The supervisor polls PIDs (≈1s cadence) and respawns any dead child without exiting.\n9:- **HTTP runtime:** **Node.js** (v24 present in the environment) using the **stdlib `http` module only** for this task—no npm registry dependency for bootstrap. One shared entrypoint, differentiated solely by `NODE_ID` / `PORT` env vars.\n10:- **Redis:** System `redis-server` (v7 present), bound to `127.0.0.1:6379`, persistence directory under `/app/data/redis`. Started as a non-daemon child of `start.sh` (no `--daemonize yes`) so the supervisor can track its PID.\n18:| Three separate start scripts | Harness expects a single foreground `/app/start.sh` |\n22:Supervisor simplicity (bash PID loop) over a real process manager: enough for marathon verification (kill + respawn windows), but no fancy backoff/jitter. Fixed ports mean `start.sh` must fail loudly if a protected harness process already owns a port rather than silently remapping.\n31:| HTTP runtime | Node.js, CommonJS or ESM; entry `server/index.js` |\n32:| Node identity | Integer `NODE_ID` ∈ {0,1,2}; `PORT = 8000 + NODE_ID` |\n34:| Durable shared state | Files under `/app/data/` (schema owned by MARATHON-3+; this task only creates dirs) |\n64:- Server: derives `node_id` only from its configured `NODE_ID` env (integer parse once at boot); does not trust client input.\n72:| HTTP node 0 | `127.0.0.1:8000` | `NODE_ID=0` |\n73:| HTTP node 1 | `127.0.0.1:8001` | `NODE_ID=1` |\n74:| HTTP node 2 | `127.0.0.1:8002` | `NODE_ID=2` |\n76:`start.sh` remains in the foreground until terminated by signal; killing an HTTP child or Redis must not stop the supervisor or the other children.\n89:| `NODE_ID` | integer 0\\|1\\|2 | yes (HTTP workers) | Stable node identity in health + future logs |\n90:| `PORT` | integer | yes (HTTP workers) | Listen port; must equal `8000 + NODE_ID` |\n94:**On-disk (created by `start.sh` if missing):**\n103:## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n106:| File | Change |\n108:| `/app/start.sh` | Executable foreground supervisor: prepare dirs, spawn Redis + 3 nodes, trap signals, poll/respawn loop, log to stdout/stderr |\n109:| `/app/server/index.js` | HTTP server entry: read `NODE_ID`/`PORT`, bind `127.0.0.1:$PORT`, route `GET /api/health`, reject invalid env at boot with non-zero exit |\n110:| `/app/server/health.js` | Pure handler building `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` (keeps routing thin for later middleware) |\n111:| `/app/package.json` | `{ \"name\": \"huddle\", \"private\": true, \"main\": \"server/index.js\" }` — documents Node entry; **no required dependencies** for this task |\n114:| File | Change |\n119:| File | Change |\n126:1. `server/health.js` + `server/index.js` (can be verified with a one-off `NODE_ID=0 PORT=8000 node server/index.js` by the implementer—architect does not run the app).\n128:3. `start.sh` (depends on server entry existing)\n129:4. Manual/QA: boot via `start.sh`, hit three health URLs, kill tests\n141:| Foreground `start.sh` | stays up, respawns | Harness lifecycle; MARATHON-19/20 extend children later |\n150:| IRC `:6667` process under same supervisor | MARATHON-20 (will extend `start.sh` to launch IRC gateway + respawn) |\n153:When MARATHON-20/21 land, they **extend** `start.sh` and the HTTP router; they must not replace the health contract or port map.\n172:No prior `start.sh`, `/api/health`, or `node_id` references exist in-repo to update.\n178:| `NODE_ID` missing or not in `{0,1,2}` | Worker prints error to stderr and exits non-zero; supervisor respawns—**implementer must pass valid env from `start.sh` so this is a programming error, not a loop** |\n179:| `PORT` missing or ≠ `8000+NODE_ID` | Same: fail fast at worker boot |\n181:| Redis already running on 6379 (foreign process) | `redis-server` fails; supervisor respawns Redis child. Log bind failure. Do not kill arbitrary PIDs outside children started by this `start.sh` (harness `marathon-freeports` is for verifiers, not the app). |\n184:| `start.sh` receives SIGINT/SIGTERM | Trap: stop respawn loop, signal/kill tracked children, then exit non-zero or 0 per convention (prefer 0 on clean TERM); do not leave orphaned node/redis children |\n188:| Double-start of `start.sh` | Second instance will fail binds; document that only one supervisor should run. No distributed lock required for marathon |\n189:| Working directory | `start.sh` `cd`s to its own directory (`/app`) so relative paths work regardless of caller cwd |\n192:## Acceptance Criteria\n194:1. Running `/app/start.sh` does not daemonize away: the script process remains in the foreground and continues until signaled.\n202:9. **MUST NOT:** remap ports; change `node_id` mapping; require Redis up for health; exit `start.sh` when a single child dies.\n207:- Boot: `/app/start.sh` in background job **only for the test harness** (script itself still runs as a foreground process in that job).\n212:- Tear down via SIGTERM to `start.sh`; confirm ports free (or document leftover only if trap failed—trap must succeed).\n216:/app/start.sh\n---\n'use strict';\n\nconst http = require('http');\nconst { sendHealth } = require('./health');\n\nfunction parseEnv() {\n  const rawId = process.env.NODE_ID;\n  const rawPort = process.env.PORT;\n\n  if (rawId === undefined || rawId === '') {\n    console.error('NODE_ID is required (0, 1, or 2)');\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const nodeId = Number(rawId);\n  if (!Number.isInteger(nodeId) || nodeId < 0 || nodeId > 2) {\n    console.error(`Invalid NODE_ID: ${rawId} (must be integer 0, 1, or 2)`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  if (rawPort === undefined || rawPort === '') {\n    console.error('PORT is required');\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const port = Number(rawPort);\n  const expected = 8000 + nodeId;\n  if (!Number.isInteger(port) || port !== expected) {\n    console.error(`PORT must equal 8000+NODE_ID (${expected}), got: ${rawPort}`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  return { nodeId, port };\n}\n\nconst { nodeId, port } = parseEnv();\n\nconst server = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n  let pathname = '/';\n  try {\n    pathname = new URL(req.url || '/', `http://127.0.0.1:${port}`).pathname;\n  } catch {\n    pathname = '/';\n  }\n\n  if (pathname === '/api/health') {\n    if (req.method === 'GET') {\n      sendHealth(res, nodeId);\n      return;\n    }\n    const body = JSON.stringify({ error: 'method_not_allowed' });\n    res.writeHead(405, {\n      'Content-Type': 'application/json; charset=utf-8',\n      'Content-Length': Buffer.byteLength(body),\n    });\n    res.end(body);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const body = JSON.stringify({ error: 'not_found' });\n  res.writeHead(404, {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json; charset=utf-8',\n    'Content-Length': Buffer.byteLength(body),\n  });\n  res.end(body);\n});\n\nserver.on('error', (err) => {\n  console.error(`[node-${nodeId}] Failed to bind 127.0.0.1:${port}: ${err.message}`);\n  process.exit(1);\n});\n\nserver.listen(port, '127.0.0.1', () => {\n  console.error(`[node-${nodeId}] listening on 127.0.0.1:${port}`);\n});\n---\n{\n  \"name\": \"huddle\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"main\": \"server/index.js\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"node --test test/*.test.js\"\n  }\n}\n---\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Huddle cluster supervisor: Redis + three HTTP nodes. Stays in the foreground.\nset -u\n\nAPP_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\ncd \"$APP_DIR\" || exit 1\n\nNODE_BIN=\"${NODE_BIN:-}\"\nif [[ -z \"$NODE_BIN\" ]]; then\n  if [[ -x /usr/bin/node ]]; then\n    NODE_BIN=/usr/bin/node\n  else\n    NODE_BIN=\"$(command -v node || true)\"\n  fi\nfi\nif [[ -z \"$NODE_BIN\" || ! -x \"$NODE_BIN\" ]]; then\n  echo \"[supervisor] node binary not found\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nREDIS_BIN=\"$(command -v redis-server || true)\"\nif [[ -z \"$REDIS_BIN\" ]]; then\n  echo \"[supervisor] redis-server not found\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nmkdir -p \"$APP_DIR/data/redis\"\n\nREDIS_PID=\"\"\ndeclare -a NODE_PIDS=(\"\" \"\" \"\")\nSHUTTING_DOWN=0\n\nprefix_stream() {\n  local prefix=\"$1\"\n  while IFS= read -r line || [[ -n \"${line:-}\" ]]; do\n    printf '%s %s\\n' \"$prefix\" \"$line\"\n  done\n}\n\nis_alive() {\n  local pid=\"${1:-}\"\n  [[ -n \"$pid\" ]] && kill -0 \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null\n}\n\nstart_redis() {\n  if [[ -f \"$APP_DIR/redis.conf\" ]]; then\n    \"$REDIS_BIN\" \"$APP_DIR/redis.conf\" \\\n      > >(prefix_stream '[redis]') 2>&1 &\n  else\n    \"$REDIS_BIN\" \\\n      --bind 127.0.0.1 \\\n      --port 6379 \\\n      --dir \"$APP_DIR/data/redis\" \\\n      --protected-mode yes \\\n      --daemonize no \\\n      --save \"\" \\\n      --appendonly no \\\n      > >(prefix_stream '[redis]') 2>&1 &\n  fi\n  REDIS_PID=$!\n  echo \"[supervisor] started redis pid=$REDIS_PID\"\n}\n\nstart_node() {\n  local id=\"$1\"\n  local port=$((8000 + id))\n  NODE_ID=\"$id\" PORT=\"$port\" \"$NODE_BIN\" \"$APP_DIR/server/index.js\" \\\n    > >(prefix_stream \"[node-$id]\") 2>&1 &\n  NODE_PIDS[$id]=$!\n  echo \"[supervisor] started node-$id pid=${NODE_PIDS[$id]} port=$port\"\n}\n\nstop_children() {\n  local pid\n  for pid in \"${NODE_PIDS[@]:-}\" \"$REDIS_PID\"; do\n    if is_alive \"$pid\"; then\n      kill \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\n    fi\n  done\n  sleep 0.2\n","localExecutionTimeMs":45},"isBackground":false},"description":"Read M2 design and sibling WIP server"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-1d75feb6-7046-4c1f-9eb9-7a9c72fbcd91-7\nfc_e5e7c324-fc01-972e-a3d1-73a11bacabe2_1","startedAtMs":"1787427390813","