00","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Fetch remaining MARATHON-21 design","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"53f7499d-d121-4e49-a5bc-a61b781ed8c4","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"loom data show MARATHON-21 -o json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint('depends:', d.get('depends_on') or d.get('dependencies'))\nprint('labels:', d.get('labels'))\nprint('status:', d.get('status'))\ndesign=d.get('design') or ''\nprint('DESIGN_LEN', len(design))\nprint(design[8000:] if len(design)>8000 else design)\n\"","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"depends: None\nlabels: ['frontend']\nstatus: in_progress\nDESIGN_LEN 20221\nter shell with `user`; keep token |\n| `401` | `localStorage.removeItem('huddle.token')`; show `#auth-modal`; clear `current-user` |\n| Network / `5xx` while booting with a token | Show auth modal **or** a non-claiming loading state, then fall back to auth modal; **MUST NOT** leave a forged `current-user` without a successful `/me` or prior successful register/login in this page life. Prefer: treat boot failure like logged-out after clear-or-keep policy — **decision: on boot network/`5xx`, keep token in storage but show a visible retry/error in the modal region and do not mark user logged-in; user can retry or clear via attempting login. On `401`, always clear token.** |\n\n---\n\n### C-SPA-5 — Logout / re-login (client-only)\n\n| Action | Behavior |\n|--------|----------|\n| Click `logout-btn` | Remove `huddle.token`; clear in-memory `user` and any shell selection state this task owns; hide authenticated chrome; show `#auth-modal` in **login** mode; clear password fields |\n| Login again (same or other user) | On `200`, store new token, show shell with new `user` |\n| “Restores workspace” meaning for **this** task | Re-entering the authenticated shell after logout→login (and after hard reload with valid token). **Domain** workspace/channel/message tree reload is **MARATHON-22**: this task exposes a stable “session became authenticated” / “session cleared” seam (e.g. `window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('huddle:auth', { detail: { user } }))` and `huddle:logout`) so 22 can refetch. Until 22 lands, shell may be empty — that is success for 21 |\n\n**MUST NOT:** call a non-existent logout API; leave `huddle.token` set after logout; show `current-user` while modal is the active unauthenticated UI.\n\n---\n\n### C-SPA-6 — DOM contract (QA / Playwright)\n\nExact attributes (implementer must not rename):\n\n| Hook | Requirement |\n|------|-------------|\n| `#auth-modal` | Present in DOM; visible when logged out; not the primary interactive surface when logged in (hidden via CSS `display:none` / `hidden` attribute / equivalent) |\n| `[data-testid=\"auth-form\"]` | The sign-up/login `<form>` inside the modal |\n| `[data-testid=\"auth-submit\"]` | Submit control (button or input) |\n| `[data-testid=\"auth-toggle\"]` | Control that switches between Sign up and Log in modes |\n| `[data-testid=\"current-user\"]` | Visible when authenticated; text identifies the user (`display_name`) |\n| `[data-testid=\"logout-btn\"]` | Visible when authenticated; triggers C-SPA-5 |\n\nForm fields (recommended stable hooks for typing; if not testid-pinned by task, use `name` attributes):\n- `name=\"username\"`, `name=\"password\"`\n- Optional `name=\"display_name\"` visible **only** in sign-up mode\n\nError surface: an element inside `#auth-modal` / `auth-form` that displays the latest error string (e.g. `data-testid=\"auth-error\"` is **recommended** for clarity but **not** required by the task text — if omitted, error text must still be visible in the modal).\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Server schema\n**No SQLite / API schema changes.** Reuses MARATHON-3 `users` / `tokens` and `UserObj`.\n\n### Browser persistence\n| Key | Type | Nullability | Notes |\n|-----|------|-------------|-------|\n| `localStorage['huddle.token']` | string | absent when logged out | Opaque bearer ≥16 chars from API; never store password |\n| In-memory `currentUser` | `UserObj` \\| null | null when logged out | Rebuilt from register/login/`/me`; not the durability source |\n\n### Backward compatibility\nAdding `GET /` HTML where unknown paths previously returned JSON `404` is an intentional behavior change for `/` and static paths only. All `/api/*` contracts remain unchanged.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `public/index.html` | SPA shell: `#auth-modal`, form with pinned testids, `#app-shell`, links to CSS/JS |\n| `public/css/app.css` | Layout for auth modal + minimal authenticated chrome; usable at 1280×900 |\n| `public/js/auth.js` | Token get/set/clear; `register` / `login` / `me` fetch helpers; Bearer header helper |\n| `public/js/app.js` | Boot, mode toggle, submit handlers, logout, show/hide modal vs shell, populate `current-user` |\n| `server/static.js` | `handleStatic(req, res, pathname) → boolean`: map `/` → `index.html`, safe file serve under `public/`, correct Content-Types |\n\n### Modify\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/index.js` | After health + auth routes, call `handleStatic`; only then JSON 404. Do not alter health/auth status codes |\n| `server/httpUtil.js` | Optional: add `sendText(res, status, body, contentType)` used by static handler — keep `sendJson`/`readJson` behavior identical |\n| `test/server.test.js` (optional but recommended) | Assert `GET /` returns `200` and `text/html` containing `auth-modal` / `data-testid=\"auth-form\"`; assert `/api/health` still JSON |\n\n### Do not modify\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/*`, `server/db.js` | Auth API owned by MARATHON-3; no logout endpoint in this task |\n| `start.sh`, `redis.conf` | Cluster bootstrap unchanged; static files need no extra process |\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\n| Workspace/channel/message UI | MARATHON-22 / 23 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Within this task\n1. `public/index.html` + CSS skeleton with pinned hooks  \n2. `server/static.js` + wire `index.js` so `GET /` works on any node  \n3. `auth.js` API helpers  \n4. `app.js` boot / submit / logout flows  \n5. Manual check: register → token in localStorage → reload → still logged in → logout → login  \n\n### Parallelism\n- Frontend implementer owns `public/**` + static routing.\n- Backend auth already closed (MARATHON-3); do not block on MARATHON-4/5.\n- MARATHON-22 **architecture/implementation** depends on: authenticated shell mount, `huddle.token`, `huddle:auth` / `huddle:logout` events (or equivalent documented callbacks), and existing testids remaining stable.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n| Seam | Downstream |\n|------|------------|\n| `GET /` HTML + static assets | QA; all SPA tasks |\n| `huddle.token` read/write/clear | MARATHON-22/23 fetch; MARATHON-18 WS `?token=` can read same key |\n| DOM testids / `#auth-modal` | QA automation |\n| Auth session events / `#app-shell` | MARATHON-22 three-pane; MARATHON-23 modals |\n\n### Build order\n- **Requires:** MARATHON-3 endpoints on the integrated head (present).\n- **Blocks:** Meaningful MARATHON-22 UI (declared dependent).\n- **Does not block:** MARATHON-4/5 backend work.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\n| Cut | Owner |\n|-----|--------|\n| Workspaces, channels, three-pane, messages, their testids | MARATHON-22 |\n| Threads, reactions, settings modals | MARATHON-23 |\n| Profile PATCH UI | MARATHON-23 (API MARATHON-4) |\n| Server token revoke / logout API | New task if ever required |\n| Client-side router for deep links beyond `/` | MARATHON-22 if needed |\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\nNeighborhood scan (`server/`, `server/auth/`, `test/`, repo greps for `localStorage`, `auth-form`, `SPA`, `static`, `index.html`):\n\n| Finding | Why excluded |\n|---------|----------------|\n| `server/auth/routes.js` register/login/me | Already implemented (MARATHON-3); consume only |\n| `server/auth/middleware.js` / tokens / users / passwords | No change |\n| `GET /api/health`, `start.sh`, Redis | MARATHON-2 |\n| `test/auth.test.js` API contract tests | Remain backend-focused; optional SPA smoke is this task only if added under Files to Modify |\n| `GET /api/users/{id}`, `PATCH /api/users/me` | MARATHON-4 |\n| Workspaces / channels / messages UI + testids | MARATHON-22 |\n| Threads / reactions / settings modals | MARATHON-23 |\n| WS subscribe / `?token=` | MARATHON-18 |\n| IRC gateway | MARATHON-20 |\n| Server-side logout / token TTL | Explicitly deferred in MARATHON-3 |\n| Email, OAuth, Slack SDK | Prohibited / unspecified |\n\nNo existing `public/` tree or `huddle.token` client code was found — greenfield SPA.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Empty username/password submit | Client may block with visible validation **or** send and show server `400`; either way user sees an error; no silent no-op |\n| Password length &lt; 8 on register | Visible error (client and/or server `400`) |\n| Duplicate username | Show server `409` `error` text in form |\n| Invalid credentials on login | Show error; stay on modal; token unset |\n| Double-click submit | Ignore second submit while request in flight (disable button) |\n| `localStorage` unavailable / throws | Show visible error that auth cannot persist; do not pretend success |\n| Stale token on boot (`401` from `/me`) | Clear `huddle.token`; show modal; no shell |\n| Boot with token, network down | Do not show a fake user; show modal or retry UI; keep token until `401` or explicit logout |\n| Logout | Token removed synchronously before UI switches; `current-user` cleared |\n| Login as user B after user A | Shell shows B’s `display_name`; no leftover A identity in chrome |\n| Hard reload while logged in | Token survives; `/me` restores shell |\n| `GET /` on `:8000`, `:8001`, `:8002` | Identical SPA (any node) |\n| Request `GET /../../etc/passwd` style path | Rejected; `404`; no file leak |\n| `POST /` | Not an API; `405` or `404`; not `500` |\n| Auth API still JSON | Static handler must not intercept `/api/*` |\n| Toggle sign-up ↔ login | Clears or retains username per UX choice; **must** clear visible error; password field cleared on toggle **recommended** |\n| Viewport 1280×900 | Auth modal and chrome fully usable; no reliance on hover-only controls for submit/logout/toggle |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/` (and `:8001`, `:8002`) returns **200** HTML for the SPA (not JSON `not_found`).\n2. HTML includes `#auth-modal` and elements with `data-testid` values **`auth-form`**, **`auth-submit`**, **`auth-toggle`**, **`current-user`**, **`logout-btn`**.\n3. From a logged-out state, user can **sign up** with valid username/password; on success they are **immediately authenticated** (modal dismissed; `current-user` shows identity) without a separate manual login step.\n4. After sign-up/login success, `localStorage.getItem('huddle.token')` is a non-empty string (length ≥ 16).\n5. Invalid register (short password, bad username) shows a **visible** error in the auth UI; user remains logged out; token **MUST NOT** be set.\n6. Login with wrong password shows a **visible** error; token **MUST NOT** be set; shell **MUST NOT** appear.\n7. `auth-toggle` switches the form between sign-up and login modes without full page navigation.\n8. Clicking `logout-btn` clears `huddle.token`, hides authenticated chrome, and shows `#auth-modal` again.\n9. After logout, logging in again returns the user to the authenticated shell (session restored for SPA purposes).\n10. Hard reload with a valid token still logged-in (via `/api/auth/me`); hard reload after logout stays logged-out.\n11. Layout is operable at **1280×900**.\n12. **MUST NOT** change `GET /api/health` or `/api/auth/*` response shapes/status codes.\n13. **MUST NOT** require `email` in the form as a mandatory field.\n14. **MUST NOT** introduce remote CDNs, Slack SDK, or a frontend build that `start.sh` must run.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (implementer)\n- Unit/integration: `GET /` → 200 + `text/html` + substring `auth-modal` / `data-testid=\"auth-form\"`.\n- Existing `test/auth.test.js` still passes (API unchanged).\n- Optional: static path traversal attempt returns 404.\n\n### Manual / browser (human or QA)\n1. Start cluster (`./start.sh`); open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` at 1280×900.\n2. Sign up `alice` / `password1` → see `current-user`, DevTools Application → `huddle.token` set.\n3. Reload → still logged in.\n4. Logout → token gone, modal visible.\n5. Login → shell returns.\n6. Toggle to sign-up, try password `short` → visible error.\n7. Repeat smoke on `:8001` (register on 8000, open 8001 with same origin storage is per-port — use login on 8001 with same credentials to prove API; note **localStorage is origin-scoped per port**, so cross-port auto-session is **not** required; cross-node token validity remains a backend property).\n\n### Explicit non-goals for verification\nWorkspace lists, messages, threads, WS — verify only auth shell + token lifecycle here.\n","stderr":"","executionTime":73,"interleavedOutput":"depends: None\nlabels: ['frontend']\nstatus: in_progress\nDESIGN_LEN 20221\nter shell with `user`; keep token |\n| `401` | `localStorage.removeItem('huddle.token')`; show `#auth-modal`; clear `current-user` |\n| Network / `5xx` while booting with a token | Show auth modal **or** a non-claiming loading state, then fall back to auth modal; **MUST NOT** leave a forged `current-user` without a successful `/me` or prior successful register/login in this page life. Prefer: treat boot failure like logged-out after clear-or-keep policy — **decision: on boot network/`5xx`, keep token in storage but show a visible retry/error in the modal region and do not mark user logged-in; user can retry or clear via attempting login. On `401`, always clear token.** |\n\n---\n\n### C-SPA-5 — Logout / re-login (client-only)\n\n| Action | Behavior |\n|--------|----------|\n| Click `logout-btn` | Remove `huddle.token`; clear in-memory `user` and any shell selection state this task owns; hide authenticated chrome; show `#auth-modal` in **login** mode; clear password fields |\n| Login again (same or other user) | On `200`, store new token, show shell with new `user` |\n| “Restores workspace” meaning for **this** task | Re-entering the authenticated shell after logout→login (and after hard reload with valid token). **Domain** workspace/channel/message tree reload is **MARATHON-22**: this task exposes a stable “session became authenticated” / “session cleared” seam (e.g. `window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('huddle:auth', { detail: { user } }))` and `huddle:logout`) so 22 can refetch. Until 22 lands, shell may be empty — that is success for 21 |\n\n**MUST NOT:** call a non-existent logout API; leave `huddle.token` set after logout; show `current-user` while modal is the active unauthenticated UI.\n\n---\n\n### C-SPA-6 — DOM contract (QA / Playwright)\n\nExact attributes (implementer must not rename):\n\n| Hook | Requirement |\n|------|-------------|\n| `#auth-modal` | Present in DOM; visible when logged out; not the primary interactive surface when logged in (hidden via CSS `display:none` / `hidden` attribute / equivalent) |\n| `[data-testid=\"auth-form\"]` | The sign-up/login `<form>` inside the modal |\n| `[data-testid=\"auth-submit\"]` | Submit control (button or input) |\n| `[data-testid=\"auth-toggle\"]` | Control that switches between Sign up and Log in modes |\n| `[data-testid=\"current-user\"]` | Visible when authenticated; text identifies the user (`display_name`) |\n| `[data-testid=\"logout-btn\"]` | Visible when authenticated; triggers C-SPA-5 |\n\nForm fields (recommended stable hooks for typing; if not testid-pinned by task, use `name` attributes):\n- `name=\"username\"`, `name=\"password\"`\n- Optional `name=\"display_name\"` visible **only** in sign-up mode\n\nError surface: an element inside `#auth-modal` / `auth-form` that displays the latest error string (e.g. `data-testid=\"auth-error\"` is **recommended** for clarity but **not** required by the task text — if omitted, error text must still be visible in the modal).\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Server schema\n**No SQLite / API schema changes.** Reuses MARATHON-3 `users` / `tokens` and `UserObj`.\n\n### Browser persistence\n| Key | Type | Nullability | Notes |\n|-----|------|-------------|-------|\n| `localStorage['huddle.token']` | string | absent when logged out | Opaque bearer ≥16 chars from API; never store password |\n| In-memory `currentUser` | `UserObj` \\| null | null when logged out | Rebuilt from register/login/`/me`; not the durability source |\n\n### Backward compatibility\nAdding `GET /` HTML where unknown paths previously returned JSON `404` is an intentional behavior change for `/` and static paths only. All `/api/*` contracts remain unchanged.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `public/index.html` | SPA shell: `#auth-modal`, form with pinned testids, `#app-shell`, links to CSS/JS |\n| `public/css/app.css` | Layout for auth modal + minimal authenticated chrome; usable at 1280×900 |\n| `public/js/auth.js` | Token get/set/clear; `register` / `login` / `me` fetch helpers; Bearer header helper |\n| `public/js/app.js` | Boot, mode toggle, submit handlers, logout, show/hide modal vs shell, populate `current-user` |\n| `server/static.js` | `handleStatic(req, res, pathname) → boolean`: map `/` → `index.html`, safe file serve under `public/`, correct Content-Types |\n\n### Modify\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/index.js` | After health + auth routes, call `handleStatic`; only then JSON 404. Do not alter health/auth status codes |\n| `server/httpUtil.js` | Optional: add `sendText(res, status, body, contentType)` used by static handler — keep `sendJson`/`readJson` behavior identical |\n| `test/server.test.js` (optional but recommended) | Assert `GET /` returns `200` and `text/html` containing `auth-modal` / `data-testid=\"auth-form\"`; assert `/api/health` still JSON |\n\n### Do not modify\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/*`, `server/db.js` | Auth API owned by MARATHON-3; no logout endpoint in this task |\n| `start.sh`, `redis.conf` | Cluster bootstrap unchanged; static files need no extra process |\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\n| Workspace/channel/message UI | MARATHON-22 / 23 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Within this task\n1. `public/index.html` + CSS skeleton with pinned hooks  \n2. `server/static.js` + wire `index.js` so `GET /` works on any node  \n3. `auth.js` API helpers  \n4. `app.js` boot / submit / logout flows  \n5. Manual check: register → token in localStorage → reload → still logged in → logout → login  \n\n### Parallelism\n- Frontend implementer owns `public/**` + static routing.\n- Backend auth already closed (MARATHON-3); do not block on MARATHON-4/5.\n- MARATHON-22 **architecture/implementation** depends on: authenticated shell mount, `huddle.token`, `huddle:auth` / `huddle:logout` events (or equivalent documented callbacks), and existing testids remaining stable.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n| Seam | Downstream |\n|------|------------|\n| `GET /` HTML + static assets | QA; all SPA tasks |\n| `huddle.token` read/write/clear | MARATHON-22/23 fetch; MARATHON-18 WS `?token=` can read same key |\n| DOM testids / `#auth-modal` | QA automation |\n| Auth session events / `#app-shell` | MARATHON-22 three-pane; MARATHON-23 modals |\n\n### Build order\n- **Requires:** MARATHON-3 endpoints on the integrated head (present).\n- **Blocks:** Meaningful MARATHON-22 UI (declared dependent).\n- **Does not block:** MARATHON-4/5 backend work.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\n| Cut | Owner |\n|-----|--------|\n| Workspaces, channels, three-pane, messages, their testids | MARATHON-22 |\n| Threads, reactions, settings modals | MARATHON-23 |\n| Profile PATCH UI | MARATHON-23 (API MARATHON-4) |\n| Server token revoke / logout API | New task if ever required |\n| Client-side router for deep links beyond `/` | MARATHON-22 if needed |\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\nNeighborhood scan (`server/`, `server/auth/`, `test/`, repo greps for `localStorage`, `auth-form`, `SPA`, `static`, `index.html`):\n\n| Finding | Why excluded |\n|---------|----------------|\n| `server/auth/routes.js` register/login/me | Already implemented (MARATHON-3); consume only |\n| `server/auth/middleware.js` / tokens / users / passwords | No change |\n| `GET /api/health`, `start.sh`, Redis | MARATHON-2 |\n| `test/auth.test.js` API contract tests | Remain backend-focused; optional SPA smoke is this task only if added under Files to Modify |\n| `GET /api/users/{id}`, `PATCH /api/users/me` | MARATHON-4 |\n| Workspaces / channels / messages UI + testids | MARATHON-22 |\n| Threads / reactions / settings modals | MARATHON-23 |\n| WS subscribe / `?token=` | MARATHON-18 |\n| IRC gateway | MARATHON-20 |\n| Server-side logout / token TTL | Explicitly deferred in MARATHON-3 |\n| Email, OAuth, Slack SDK | Prohibited / unspecified |\n\nNo existing `public/` tree or `huddle.token` client code was found — greenfield SPA.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Empty username/password submit | Client may block with visible validation **or** send and show server `400`; either way user sees an error; no silent no-op |\n| Password length &lt; 8 on register | Visible error (client and/or server `400`) |\n| Duplicate username | Show server `409` `error` text in form |\n| Invalid credentials on login | Show error; stay on modal; token unset |\n| Double-click submit | Ignore second submit while request in flight (disable button) |\n| `localStorage` unavailable / throws | Show visible error that auth cannot persist; do not pretend success |\n| Stale token on boot (`401` from `/me`) | Clear `huddle.token`; show modal; no shell |\n| Boot with token, network down | Do not show a fake user; show modal or retry UI; keep token until `401` or explicit logout |\n| Logout | Token removed synchronously before UI switches; `current-user` cleared |\n| Login as user B after user A | Shell shows B’s `display_name`; no leftover A identity in chrome |\n| Hard reload while logged in | Token survives; `/me` restores shell |\n| `GET /` on `:8000`, `:8001`, `:8002` | Identical SPA (any node) |\n| Request `GET /../../etc/passwd` style path | Rejected; `404`; no file leak |\n| `POST /` | Not an API; `405` or `404`; not `500` |\n| Auth API still JSON | Static handler must not intercept `/api/*` |\n| Toggle sign-up ↔ login | Clears or retains username per UX choice; **must** clear visible error; password field cleared on toggle **recommended** |\n| Viewport 1280×900 | Auth modal and chrome fully usable; no reliance on hover-only controls for submit/logout/toggle |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/` (and `:8001`, `:8002`) returns **200** HTML for the SPA (not JSON `not_found`).\n2. HTML includes `#auth-modal` and elements with `data-testid` values **`auth-form`**, **`auth-submit`**, **`auth-toggle`**, **`current-user`**, **`logout-btn`**.\n3. From a logged-out state, user can **sign up** with valid username/password; on success they are **immediately authenticated** (modal dismissed; `current-user` shows identity) without a separate manual login step.\n4. After sign-up/login success, `localStorage.getItem('huddle.token')` is a non-empty string (length ≥ 16).\n5. Invalid register (short password, bad username) shows a **visible** error in the auth UI; user remains logged out; token **MUST NOT** be set.\n6. Login with wrong password shows a **visible** error; token **MUST NOT** be set; shell **MUST NOT** appear.\n7. `auth-toggle` switches the form between sign-up and login modes without full page navigation.\n8. Clicking `logout-btn` clears `huddle.token`, hides authenticated chrome, and shows `#auth-modal` again.\n9. After logout, logging in again returns the user to the authenticated shell (session restored for SPA purposes).\n10. Hard reload with a valid token still logged-in (via `/api/auth/me`); hard reload after logout stays logged-out.\n11. Layout is operable at **1280×900**.\n12. **MUST NOT** change `GET /api/health` or `/api/auth/*` response shapes/status codes.\n13. **MUST NOT** require `email` in the form as a mandatory field.\n14. **MUST NOT** introduce remote CDNs, Slack SDK, or a frontend build that `start.sh` must run.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (implementer)\n- Unit/integration: `GET /` → 200 + `text/html` + substring `auth-modal` / `data-testid=\"auth-form\"`.\n- Existing `test/auth.test.js` still passes (API unchanged).\n- Optional: static path traversal attempt returns 404.\n\n### Manual / browser (human or QA)\n1. Start cluster (`./start.sh`); open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` at 1280×900.\n2. Sign up `alice` / `password1` → see `current-user`, DevTools Application → `huddle.token` set.\n3. Reload → still logged in.\n4. Logout → token gone, modal visible.\n5. Login → shell returns.\n6. Toggle to sign-up, try password `short` → visible error.\n7. Repeat smoke on `:8001` (register on 8000, open 8001 with same origin storage is per-port — use login on 8001 with same credentials to prove API; note **localStorage is origin-scoped per port**, so cross-port auto-session is **not** required; cross-node token validity remains a backend property).\n\n### Explicit non-goals for verification\nWorkspace lists, messages, threads, WS — verify only auth shell + token lifecycle here.\n","localExecutionTimeMs":33},"isBackground":false},"description":"Fetch remaining MARATHON-21 design"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-9b358185-13c3-4ccd-8e39-0192ca88096e-10\nfc_67d0be31-ef79-9454-812a-d329d8f23db9_0","startedAtMs":"1787428499200","completedAtMs":"1787428499273"},"model_call_id":"c58c3af0-527e-4f9f-a18d-0824a3aed063-3-fncl","session_id":"53f7499d-d121-4e49-a5bc-a61b781ed8c4","timestamp_ms":1787428499322}
